For each event, we can perform the jet \(p_{T}\) and mass corrections using the different settings and methods listed above. We then calculate the dijet invariant mass differences between these samples relative to the default standard setting (MLP). The results from different machine learning methods (LD and k-NN) and the different MLP settings (test 1, test 2, test 3) were added in quadrature. The square root of the quadrature sum is the final systematic error.

